{
 "version": 1,
 "_about": "(polish1 item 26) THE BHOP SERVER: the hop island became a CS-style bhop server. `hub` = the floating plaza you arrive on (world metres, y = its top), with one gate per stage `type` round it (name, colour) and three portals each; `exit` = where on the hub the arch back to the islands stands. `stages`: 6 types x 3 tiers; each has an `id` (saved best times are kept by it), a `name`, a `tier` (1 easy .. 3 hard) and a `recipe` that core/bhop_stages.gd turns into its platforms: fixed = data/course.json (today's course is classic 1); hops = pads one after another (`pads`, pad size, edge-to-edge `gap` range, `turn` degrees between hops (alternate = left / right), `rise` up / down range, a checkpoint every `every` pads, `speed` / `strafe` = what the hops are built for, as in course.json); surf = slanted ramps (`ramps`, `length`, `angle` from the ground, `drop` per ramp, `gap` between, `width`, `bend` degrees the run turns); long = long jumps off runways (`jumps` gaps in metres, `runway`, `landing`, `width`); climb = KZ: blocks that rise (`rise` range per step, `gap`, `block` size) with LADDERS between (metres tall each); edgebug = Source-style edgebugs (`drops` floors, `fall` metres floor to floor, a `pillar` that tall and `block` wide on each floor, `reach` = metres from the ledge you leave to the pillar's near face, `floor` size, `edge` = how lenient the pillar's edge is: 0.707 = only a true edge contact, nearer 1 = a wider band round it). `edgebug` (units/s): on edgebug stages a landing faster than `hard_landing` sends you back (Source's safe fall speed is about 580); clipping an edge while falling faster than `min_fall` stops the fall there and pushes you off the edge at `push`. `seed` makes a stage the same for everyone. `ring` = how far from the hub the stages stand; `fall_below` as in course.json; `ladder_speed` (units/s) climbing.",
